@@ -433,6 +433,17 @@ Hypercurve separates exact values from decisions about them:
   scalar refinement, coefficient growth, allocation, or wall-clock time. The
   [accounting module](../hypersolve/src/work_budget.rs) lists the coverage and
   remaining gaps; the full per-operation bound remains an open target.
+- Native intersection batches retain owned circle-support relations for one
+  synchronous operation under one predicate policy. Batches of up to eight
+  retained entries use ordered equality lookup. Larger batches index exact
+  rational centers and squared radii when their scalar storage class is not
+  `VeryLarge`; symbolic and very large supports retain ordered equality lookup.
+  These cost choices do not restrict supported inputs. Earlier unindexed entries
+  keep their original matching priority. Hits reuse the same relation and ordered
+  witnesses. The cache has no eviction or configurable disable switch and is
+  released when the batch is dropped. Its entry count, key storage, and scalar
+  payloads have no internal heap-byte or total-work bound; it is not shared
+  between independent operations or threads.
 - `CurvePreviewOptions` owns finite display tolerances separately. Operations
   called inside `evaluate` use its edge-preview context; its scoped preview
   results are never exact topology or construction provenance.
